-- The DISPATCH half of an alias-qualified method occurrence: which impl's body
-- actually RUNS, as opposed to whether an impl obligation exists for it at all
-- (the CHECKED half, #1276/#1386, pinned by the sibling rows in this file).
-- `Blob` implements BOTH `IA` and `IB`, and `A.mth Blob` / `B.mth Blob` are two
-- alias-qualified calls naming TWO DIFFERENT interfaces.
--
-- Hand-derived answer: 1 then 2 — each call dispatches to the impl its own alias
-- names.  That is what all three verbs now produce.  The row was a KNOWN-BAD
-- ledger entry until #1386's supply fix stopped `renameAliasedMethods` erasing
-- `A.mth` to a bare `mth` before dispatch was decided: with the spelling gone,
-- both occurrences asked `admittedIfaceFor "mth"`, whose answer is one
-- last-write-wins row, so both collapsed onto ONE impl on check, run and build
-- alike.  It pinned (1,1) when the floor resolved to `IA` and (2,2) after
-- `cdca5045` moved the floor to `IB` -- one of two wrong either way.  The
-- occurrence now keeps its spelling through inference, `admittedIfaceFor`
-- answers per spelling from the alias supply, and the row's method-set
-- membership is looked up under the ORIGIN name, so the two calls no longer
-- share a decision.
--
-- This is the acceptance case for that split.  It does not close #1182/#1265,
-- whose subject is a BARE occurrence with two admitted declarations and no
-- spelling to tell them apart; nothing here gives that shape a discriminator.
-- A value change is a regression in the alias-spelling channel: the two
-- projections `ieSelectRowByMethod` makes off one occurrence name -- the
-- interface from the SPELLING, the row's method-set membership from the ORIGIN
-- -- coming apart is the shape that would cause it, and it is silent, since
-- this program is accepted on every verb whichever impl runs.
import ifa.{IA}
import ifb.{IB}
import ifa as A
import ifb as B

public export data Blob = Blob

export impl IA Blob where
  mth b = 1

export impl IB Blob where
  mth b = 2

main =
  let _ = println (A.mth Blob)
  println (B.mth Blob)
